    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced for JPM. The bull case is strong on fundamentals: JPM is the highest-quality U.S. bank with a fortress balance sheet ($317B equity, 8.1% equity-to-assets) and is in a confirmed uptrend with price above all key moving averages and positive MACD. However, the bear's timing concerns are equally valid: RSI at 81.95 is deeply overbought, the MACD histogram has collapsed 87.5% (+0.72 to +0.09), and there is a bearish divergence (RSI lower high vs. price higher high). At $163.46, the risk/reward is poor \u2014 roughly 8% downside to the rising 50 SMA (~$150) vs. only ~4% upside to the $170 target. Sentiment and news data are UNAVAILABLE as of the historical as-of date and should not be treated as a signal. Given the balanced evidence, the correct action is to maintain existing positions \u2014 not to add aggressively at the top of a 60-day run, and not to exit a quality name in a confirmed uptrend. For existing holders, tighten stops to just below the 10 EMA (~$160.50) to protect the 19% 60-day gains. For new capital, wait for a pullback toward the rising 50 SMA ($148-$152) for a materially better risk/reward entry.\n\n**Entry Price**: 150.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 160.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-market weight. If adding on a pullback to $148-$152, size conservatively (no more than 25-33% of intended full position at first tranche).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
